An unlock that hands the turn to the thread that paid for it, which pays for it still.
A turn's payer is the turn's own thread.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a turn's payer is not another thread of its core

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -713,7 +713,6 @@ void sched_mutex_unlock(struct mutex *m)
      */
     struct thread *was = core->turn;
     w->state = THREAD_READY;
-    core->payer = NULL;
     core->turn = w;
     thread_settle(was);
     thread_settle(w);
